error_signature: "error: non-constant-expression cannot be narrowed from type 'signed char' to 'char' in initializer list.*\\[-Wc++11-narrowing\\]"
root_cause: "clang 15 turns -Wc++11-narrowing into a hard error for the C++ that sip generates for test/module_attrs (it initialises char from a signed-char expression). Upstream targets GCC/MSVC where this is only a warning, so the generated code is valid there but rejected here."
rec_approach: "Export CXXFLAGS with -Wno-c++11-narrowing when running the upstream test suite: `CXXFLAGS='-Wno-c++11-narrowing' python3 -m pytest test/`. This only relaxes the diagnostic for the test build; the packaged module is unaffected. Alternative if it ever matters for a shipped artifact: const_cast to unsigned char in the .sip — but do not patch upstream for a diagnostic-only difference."
match_keywords: ["Wc++11-narrowing", "non-constant-expression cannot be narrowed", "signed char", "char", "module_attrs", "sip"]
severity:               1
category: toolchain
